# Test: ze doctor --json reports an IPsec config the host's kernel cannot carry
# VALIDATES: the ike engine's kernel capability enrolment is reachable from the
# USER entry point -- registration, phase filtering, platform filtering and the
# diagnostic code all have to line up for this to emit anything. The verdict is
# an ERROR now, so `ze doctor` exits 1 and the daemon refuses to start on the
# same enrolment (plan/immediate/spec-kernel-capability-gate.md AC-2, AC-3).
# PREVENTS: the silent failure the check exists for. Every other IPsec surface
# reports what the engine believed at install time, so a host that cannot carry a
# single SA still shows a tunnel as up and carries nothing.
# Required by ai/rules/repo-maintenance.md ("Test Requirement": unit AND
# functional), mirroring test/ui/doctor-ipsec-cookie-threshold.ci.

# The probe is forced to the absent answer so the diagnostic is reached on a host
# whose kernel is healthy. Without the override this test would pass only where
# XFRM happens to be absent, which is the vacuity trap of
# ai/rules/interop-and-goal-validation.md.
option=env:var=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm:value=absent

tmpfs=ipsec-xfrm.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
    ipsec {
        interface lo
        ike-group IKE-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
                hash sha256
                dh-group 14
            }
        }
        esp-group ESP-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
            }
        }
        site-to-site {
            peer branch {
                connection-type respond
                remote-address 203.0.113.7
                ike-group IKE-1
                esp-group ESP-1
                authentication {
                    mode pre-shared-secret
                    pre-shared-secret correct-horse-battery-staple
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json ipsec-xfrm.conf
# Exit 1: an absent capability makes the host not ready, and the daemon refuses.
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unavailable
# The netlink failure must reach the operator. A message that says the dataplane is
# unavailable and nothing about the cause names no action.
expect=stdout:contains=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze explain doctor-ipsec-xfrm-unavailable
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=CONFIG_INET_ESP
